reason:
I reproduced both holes against the current code, using a scratch --store so the repo's record store was not touched. (1) An empty --transcripts dir with --record printed transcriptsScanned 0 and stored a bench:trace-bench-lite record with final_status accept and no F0. (2) A leaking transcript with no meta (label '') maps to arm 'unknown'. markContaminated never matches it, so contaminatedRuns stays 0 and no F0 is raised. In the held-verdict variant the stored record was accept with failed_gates [], which clears the F0/F4 conditions of the L3 checklist gate. Existing tests cover only the missing-flag case and a well-formed verifier label.

I also found a third hole that strengthens the finding. The panel label regex at lib.mjs:934 uses `[a-z-]+`, so a correctly labelled leak from the production 'qa-e2e' critic is also unattributable. The fix should widen that class to `[a-z0-9-]+`, in addition to:
- requiring transcripts.length > 0, ideally at least the number of runs, for --record;
- treating any 'unknown' key as an F0 (fail-closed) flag;
- adding tests for the empty-dir, unknown-label and qa-e2e-label cases.

Severity 'important' is justified because the L3 trust gate relies on this record.
